{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "Ordered per-platform builder phase tables that map `==> ` banner lines to a determinate step-K-of-M progress estimate. Data-driven (not code) so the admin-bff pod-log follower ports the SAME tables + regexes for web progress parity (design 2.9 / spec 10).",
    "source": "The `banner \"...\"` call sites in each build-<platform>-stage4.sh, in source order. A drift probe (test_progress_parse.py) greps those call sites per builder and asserts the count equals the total number of match patterns here, so a builder banner change fails CI until this file is updated.",
    "banner_regex": "^==>\\s*(.*)$",
    "ansi_regex": "\\x1b\\[[0-9;]*[A-Za-z]",
    "emerge_regex": ">>> (?:Emerging|Installing) \\((\\d+) of (\\d+)\\)",
    "failure_regex": "^\\s*!!",
    "matching": "A phase is reached when a banner line contains ANY of that phase's `any` substrings. Matching is forward-only (monotonic): the parser advances to the earliest not-yet-passed phase whose pattern matches, so conditional/SKIPPED banners never regress the bar. Alternative banners for the SAME boundary (e.g. 'Installing mesh VPN' vs 'Mesh VPN SKIPPED') are grouped into one phase but counted as distinct patterns for the drift probe."
  },
